 R←Test_Server_120(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;c;q;r;noOf;before;new;report;html
⍝ Ask for the "crash" page.
⍝ Besides HandleError's own files, the request must be saved next to them, without its credentials.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '∘∘∘ ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 :If ##.FilesAndDirs.IsDir ∆GetCrashFolder
     noOf←≢##.FilesAndDirs.ListFiles ∆GetCrashFolder
     before←##.FilesAndDirs.ListFiles ∆GetCrashFolder,'/*.request.json'
 :Else
     noOf←0
     before←''
 :EndIf

 c←∆NewClient
 q←Rumba.NewRequest 0
 q.RequestTarget←'/crash'
 q.Headers,←⊂'Authorization' 'Bearer Test_Server_120-secret'
 r←c Rumba.SendAndReceive q

 →T.PassesIf r.StatusCode=500
 →T.PassesIf∨/'<h1>500: Internal Server Error</h1>'⍷r.Content
 →T.PassesIf(noOf+3)=≢##.FilesAndDirs.ListFiles ∆GetCrashFolder

 new←(##.FilesAndDirs.ListFiles ∆GetCrashFolder,'/*.request.json')~before
 →T.PassesIf 1=≢new
 html←⊃⎕NGET(¯13↓⊃new),'.html'                  ⍝ `.request.json` is 13 characters
 →T.PassesIf~∨/'customFns failed'⍷html          ⍝ HandleError notes a failing customFns there
 →T.PassesIf∨/'Full request in'⍷html            ⍝ `SaveCrashRequest` points at its file ...
 →T.PassesIf∨/'GET /crash'⍷html                 ⍝ ... and summarizes the request
 report←⎕JSON⊃⎕NGET⊃new
 →T.PassesIf'/crash'≡(⊃report.Messages).RequestTarget
 →T.PassesIf~∨/'Test_Server_120-secret'⍷⊃⎕NGET⊃new
 →T.PassesIf(⊂'authorization' '***')∊(⊃report.Messages).Headers

 R←T._OK
⍝Done
